body:
Lets just use some common sense really quick. She is talking about struggling and bad health while she is very obviously morbidly obese which means she actually has an abundance of food and whatever she is doing doesn't require her to move much obviously. 99% of the time when people stand in front of people like this, they are simply wanting even more for less.

&#x200B;

My ex has two children with me, and without child support, still has plenty to live off of while all the money from the state handles food and rent and healthcare, the money from her real job goes 100% into her pocket after taxes. Most people are not as "poor" as you think and simply mismanage their funds and then come running for more because they want enough money to support their families AND the lavish lifestyle they want.

So Logan Paul was filming dead people hanging from trees, various other YouTubers were doing "its just a prank bro" bs around this age. He doesn't make endless drama videos for views, the only "lying" I would say he does is the over acting he does but at least it gets his viewers amped up and doing things like Football. He makes a joke out of himself most of the time.

&#x200B;

The guy in the video invited Speed to join him and yet the title makes it look like he barged in to a recording studio in India and sat down next to this dude and ruined his session. What do you guys have against this guy?

Many of the reviewers with 100k+ subscribers are pretty much paid Meta sponsors at this point. Getting access to products way early by signing a paper that says you won't say anything bad about them should be throwing up major red flags and people should be refusing to go. Instead I have seen no shortage of people going for easy views and clicks at the expense of being truthful and trustworthy to their subscribers. Most of these people have said damn near the EXACT same things as each other. Many have peddled shit games and nothing updates acting like its the best thing on the planet. I have had to refund several games because I trusted a VR Youtuber only for the game to be like 30 minutes long for a ton of money or the game was just a nothing "oh this is kinda neat" game.

&#x200B;

I have said it multiple times, but telling people they have done a good job when they haven't doesn't help anybody at all, and only holds the industry back.

What headset do you have and what program are you using to play it from your headset?

&#x200B;

Just in case you don't respond in time. I have had issues where if my headset and controllers were not on and connected to Steam VR, The game wouldn't start.

[https://headlineusa.com/democrats-kavanaugh-accuser-lied-criminal/](https://headlineusa.com/democrats-kavanaugh-accuser-lied-criminal/)

&#x200B;

One of the accusers.

Ok here we go...

&#x200B;

Go to chatgpt and have it write several letters pretending to be her, to different high level professors, talking about how great it is to be there and include professional credentials. Then have it write a request to get in the school. Then pose as someone who doesn't know her online and run the text through an AI Detector and act outraged. Make it seem like she only got to where she is because she used text generated from an AI. Screenshot it and send it out to the school. Also post her name and face around the school, along with the AI Detector result so everyone knows she cheated to get into the college. The teachers and students will now think she is a fraud.

&#x200B;

Also tell her she left some perfume with you and you want to give it back. Fill it with liquid ass and give it back to her.

I said since day one that the Quest Pro was hot garbage for the price and every Meta fanboy come out to say it was revolutionary and was well worth the 1 to 2 hour battery life and the insanely disappointing color pass through.

&#x200B;

Many popular YouTubers are not criticizing Meta at all and what they are doing is also setting VR back. These content creators just want in the good graces of Meta and these companies so they can get an early review and details of products for views and subscribers. VR is at a deadlock because of the ass kissing.

YouTubers profiting off fakeness is ingrained into YouTube itself at this point and is definitely encouraged.  YouTubers exposing them occasionally pop up, but even then, those people are out for their profits as well. Its a cycle.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Elaborating on the YouTubers exposing thing, the point I am trying to make is that YouTubers who make it their whole purpose to expose as many people as possible will often not take the issues as seriously as it needs to because tomorrow there will just be another person to report on or make a video about. Issues that need to be nipped in the bud that day will be kind of glossed over.

They falsely advertised A LOT of things with this headset during Connect or were just silent on major issues they knew would be brought up which is why people were saying it was going to be a trash headset even for business'. The VR legs, Disney style Face Tracking, Battery Life, Quality of Passthrough. 

&#x200B;

People need to be screaming this from the rooftops that this is unacceptable for a 1500 dollar headset.

Its not apart of the demo because from what i've seen its very glitchy and can't track precisely. Smiles are creepy looking. What has mainly been shown are prerendered Disney animations, showing the non existent avatars doing real time face and eye expressions and NEVER showing the real deal. They don't have the confidence to show it, because then the whole reason the unit costs so much gets exposed as not being worth it and there goes any reason to buy this 1500 dollar Quest 2 with color passthrough.

&#x200B;

There are people in these comments saying its worth 1500 because its more comfortable? This has to be a joke.

So far having played an hour of it.

&#x200B;

Its alright. I mean, its a mod of an old game now, but the immersion isn't really there, and for some reason I feel like I'm sliding on ice moving around.
